From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:46:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: ipad5: Enable USB host on the Lightning
 port

Enable the S8000 USB role switch on the iPad 5 with the D2365 PMIC
(accessory power LDO) and the Tristar (ACC pin routing), and point the
Lightning charger at it, so that its accessory policy can give the port
to the host controllers while the camera adapter is attached. The
charger keeps setting the device controller's role through its port.

Tested on an iPad 5 (J71t) with the Lightning to USB camera adapter:
attaching it switches the port to the host role with EHCI and OHCI up;
USB mass storage transfers at about 36 MB/s; a powered USB-C hub
enumerates with its hub, SD card reader and RTL8152 Ethernet; detaching
the adapter returns the port to the device role and restores the USB
gadget.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
index 8f19a2f0d..8529ac608 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
@@ -204,6 +204,7 @@ tristar_charger: charger@180 {
 				     <72 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
 				     <77 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 			apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
+			apple,usb-role-switch = <&usb_role>;
 			input-current-limit-microamp = <2400000>;
 
 			/* The charger decides when USB data may come on. */
@@ -477,3 +478,10 @@ usbdev_role: endpoint {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/* Lightning host role: accessory power from LDO5, ACC routing by the Tristar. */
+&usb_role {
+	apple,pmic = <&d2365_pmic>;
+	apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
